      "message": "I’ve managed to isolate the reproduction steps!\n\nSteps:\n\nConnect Bluetooth headphones (tested with JBL Live 675NC on Pixel 7a)\n\nPlay media (specifically tested with YouTube Shorts)\n\nAllow the battery to drain until the device forces a shutdown (I used 4K60 video recording to accelerate the battery drain beforehand)\n\nObservations:\n\nAudio Fallback: As the Bluetooth stack shuts down, audio briefly routes through the device speakers before the system fully kills the power.\n\nStuttering: I noticed the audio cut in and out multiple times once - but haven\u0027t been able to reproduce that specific issue since.\n\nIsolation: I verified that if the video is paused and no BT is connected, the audio does not play during low-battery shutdown.",
